hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to the  edition of ask Evan today I'm going to  answer a question from one of our  Twitter readers his name is Kyle Kyle  Van Pelt and he wrote in saying how do  you determine what adds the most value  to your business listen to the question  Kyle I think I may mention this before  but on my way to work every day I try to  ask myself what can I do to add the most  value to my business today and I find  that if I'm doing things too much that  is not adding a lot of value I try to  see does this still need to be done and  if so does it have to be me who's doing  it and again as you're walking to your  office or however you're going in if  you're waking up and you're going off to  your chair if you're working from home  you do want to think how can I add the  most value to my business now in terms  of how to determine that for me what I  do is to think about impact and the two  impacts that I can have is one helping  one person or one client and having it  in a really meaningful way and so  spending you know a lot of time going  in-depth adding a lot of value to help  one person and hopefully touch them you  know change your life or change their  business and have a really strong impact  the other form of impact I find is is  hitting more masses so having a slightly  less strong connection but still be able  to help and reach a lot of people so  example the first one I might help a  client or might help an entrepreneur  one-on-one if it's a coffee meeting and  just try to really dig into their  business and give them some advice the  example of the second one is is doing  videos like this right I'm in my house I  don't I'm talking to a whole bunch of  people hi but I'm never going to meet  most of you but hopefully there's still  some kind of impact that I can have and  give some advice encourage your  motivation ideas to help you grow your  business so when I'm walking to the  office or try to think how can I have  the most impact how can I add the most  value  if I look at some of the things  especially most entrepreneurs if you're  doing a lot of admin work or accounting  work as an example if you do in your  books how much impact does that have  right are you helping people you're  helping one person really in-depth are  you helping a lot of people in a less  impactful way but you're helping more  people at the same time probably not so  there's a lot of things that you're  probably doing that is not helping  people is not having a big impact that  may still need to get done you know so  for me the books have to get done at my  company there's a lot of admin work that  has to get done it doesn't mean that I  have to do it and you want to try to get  to the point where you can either you  eliminate the stuff you don't need  automate as much as possible and then  delegate the work that still has to get  done by somebody but shouldn't always be  you so for these videos for example my  brand is me so I'm on the videos i want  to help answer the question you know you  tweeted me with a question so i want to  answer that personally that's not  something I can hand off to somebody and  say hey Kyle great question here's my  assistant is going to answer for you  right I want to try to make that a  little more personal but there are the  things that I can hand off that I have a  great team and they can manage do on the  run without me so you got to play that  you know I guess that balance and figure  out what should be done by you where  you're adding a lot of value versus what  can be handed off to the people on your  team at the start you know you may not  have a lot of money to hire somebody the  first person I hired was for one hour a  day you don't have to have somebody  full-time you don't have to have  somebody come to your office into your  home it can be part-time really small  you know an hour a day a couple hours a  week just to unload some of the work  that you're doing and give you more time  to free up working on bigger projects  that can help grow your business another  thing I think about when I try to think  about adding value is I like starting  projects and not running project so i'll  get something going i'll come up with a  lot of new ideas that's my main role at  the company now I guess is coming up  with ways to grow the business and all  launching I'll spend a lot of time  testing things out and then once I have  the system  kind of humming I'll hand it off to my  team to continue to run with and then  I'm off to the new project if you're  thinking about value for your business  especially if you want to sell it you  want to have a business that can run  without you in it as much as possible so  you have systems procedures a team in  place structure that the business can  run without you having to be there and  so as much as possible to remove myself  from the day-to-day operations of the  business and focus on new growth and for  me that's adding a lot of value to the  business so I don't know what stage  you're at with your company at the  moment but you want to try to at least  carve out some time every week I call a  CEO time where you're focusing on  projects that will grow the business and  not just running the operations of the  company hopefully I'll helped answer  your question is a great question i  really enjoyed that one for those of you  watching if you liked it please give it  a thumbs up below makes going to do more  of these videos and i love here we have  to think if you want to leave a comment  under the video about how you know how  you determine value and what what tasks  add the most value for you and if you  have a question for your own business  I'd love to try to answer it for you on  leave in the comments section below I  love seeing that come in and love to  hear your thoughts if you won't leave a  comment below so thank you and I'll see  you on the next episode  you
 

